# Ruby Conventions

- Follow RuboCop (150 character max line length)
- Use compact `module/class` definitions; avoid nested styles
- Error handling: use custom exceptions in `lib/custom_exceptions/`
- Models: validate presence/uniqueness, add proper indexes
- Controllers: use strong params

## Specs

- Prefer `with_modified_env` over stubbing `ENV` directly
- In parallel/reloading environments, compare `error.class.name` instead of constant class equality

## Example

```ruby
# ❌ BAD
module Foo
  class Bar
  end
end

# ✅ GOOD
class Foo::Bar
end
```
